%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ca23d3e41cd5424c9ec72c610ef25a4, type: 3}
  m_Name: GoodMoniHH_2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  autoFocusSpeaker: 1
  screens:
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (A point? About what?)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267874930425962
    - rid: 4351267874930425963
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: About how becoming a better person requires deliberate focus and effort.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267874930425974
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (So what? "Improving my behavior" is just supposed to sweep everything
      under the rug?)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (They don't even know what I did, <i>what I would've done</i>...)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267874930425983
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: You're not thinking about it right.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267874930425984
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (How?!? Which part?)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267874930425985
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: You're thinking in terms of "payback" and "guilt," as if you committed
      a crime and need to be sent to jail for it.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (But I <i>did</i> do something wrong!)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267874930425986
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Sure, but you're only considering punitive justice as valid.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267874930425987
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (Huh? What do you mean?)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267874930425988
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: 'Well, punitive justice is what most people think of when they think
      of justice:'
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267874930425993
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: You commit a crime, or wrong somebody, your guilt is determined, and
      then you are sentenced to a punishment to pay for it.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Whether that be a fine, or jail time, or something else.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: But, what's missing from that picture is the victims.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: If someone steals something from a store, and sells what they stole,
      does the store owner receive justice when the criminal is jailed?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: The potential profit/investment is still lost, whether or not the criminal
      is jailed or not.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: So, would some form of punishment really bring justice to the other girls?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (...)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267874930425994
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (... no.)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267874930425995
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Then you should stop thinking in terms of punitive justice, and start
      thinking in terms of restorative justice.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267874930425996
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (...?)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Oh come on, you're the president of a literature club; use your context
      clues!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267874930425997
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Restorative justice is about restoring the losses to the victims, not
      that it's always possible to completely reverse a crime.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267874930425999
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: So instead of thinking about the equivalent suffering you should endure,
      think of the equivalent good you should give.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (...)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (... okay.)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267874930426000
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (You should probably check in with the others.)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ({mc} and I have had your attention for a while now, ahaha!)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267874930426001
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Of course.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (Goodbye, sweetie...)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267874930426004
    - rid: 4351267874930426005
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions: []
